| 2026-08-02 | FIX-P0 | **`/dashboard` rendered a blank white page — reported as a P0 regression, fixed, and made structurally impossible.** **Two mistakes met.** **(1)** The header's Dashboard button linked every signed-in user to a literal `/dashboard` — a path **§14.1 does not define**. The sitemap lists *role-specific* homes (`/dashboard/student`, `/dashboard/parent`, `/teacher`, `/admin`), and §4.1b step 4a calls the post-login landing a "role-based dashboard redirect" for exactly that reason. **(2)** The path switch's `default` branch returned **`null`**, so React rendered nothing and the browser showed an empty document — the outcome §14.4 forbids outright (*"never a blank page, never a crash"*). Every unknown URL behaved the same way; the button merely guaranteed someone found it, **in one click, from every page**. **A third, quieter defect sat behind them:** `AdminRouter`'s `AdminNotFound` was **unreachable** — `main.tsx` reaches it only when `isAdminPath(path)` is true, and `isAdminPath` *is* `moduleForPath(path) !== null`, so its null check could never fire. The application had a not-found page no path could reach, and none for the paths that needed one. **The fix makes the invariant checkable instead of trusting a switch statement:** the routing decision is now `resolveRoute(path)` in `lib/route.ts`, a pure function over a closed `Route` union, and `main.tsx` only maps a decision to a component. **`roleHomePath(roles)`** resolves the button's target most-privileged-role-first, and returns `null` for a role-less account so the button is **hidden** rather than pointing nowhere (§14.4 R16 puts that account on the no-permission state). **Two states kept deliberately distinct:** `not-found` (§14.1 does not define this path) and `screen-pending` (§14.1 *does* define it; no milestone has built it) — collapsing them would tell a teacher their home is *gone* when it is merely unbuilt, the same distinction the back office already draws with `ModulePending`. **Both